[17592186285810 1034 "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}y" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285810 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285810 1111 #uuid "2a065bab-a3f3-5969-a499-32bec8351be0" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285811 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285812 13194139534391 true] [17592186285811 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285814 13194139534391 true] [17592186285811 1089 "q-274746" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285811 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534391 true] [17592186285811 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997987/assets/cdd531ad1df161f1c345c053c51e70fb522178f83688d1bdd07096bbdd40df00.png)\n\nDetermine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the above parabola. Express your answer in the form $x=2pt,y=p{t}^{2},$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285811 1113 #uuid "716f582f-6ae3-52fc-944d-f0627997e4ba" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285811 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(4,2).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(4,2),$ we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=2$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4=2pt \\\\ 2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(2)t,\\,y=(2){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=4t,\\,y=2{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285813 13194139534391 true] [17592186285812 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534391 true] [17592186285812 1041 "field-1" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285812 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285813 13194139534391 true] [17592186285812 1110 #uuid "85147514-3354-58a7-a1e6-279ac135e7ab" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285813 1034 "4t" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285813 1111 #uuid "2d42c5d5-80e3-580d-960e-7df227493003" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285815 13194139534391 true] [17592186285814 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534391 true] [17592186285814 1041 "field-2" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285814 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285815 13194139534391 true] [17592186285814 1110 #uuid "50614bfe-72ab-557f-b670-366e2ddcee47" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285815 1034 "2t^2" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285815 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285815 1111 #uuid "be5cba92-c81d-5562-a82c-b4204abed9f0" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285816 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285817 13194139534391 true] [17592186285816 1089 "q-274758" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285816 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534391 true] [17592186285816 1100 "Consider the following parabola:\n\n$$\nx=5{t}^{2},\\,y=10t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the parabola is\n\n${y}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534391 true] [17592186285816 1113 #uuid "f800c495-45f0-573d-8c95-cc345545ac2f" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285816 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x}{5},\\,t=\\frac{y}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\