capture/13997987/assets/d8e4aa88acf2a0d69d4c4208dc4951a33cc92e59e177395ec74be3ae0f9a8c7f.png)\n\nDetermine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the parabola shown above. Express your answer in the form $x=p{t}^{2},y=2pt,$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285830 1113 #uuid "864c98fc-1abc-5908-a417-e5cb64cfdbb7" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285830 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-5,-4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-5,-4),$ we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=-4$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5=p{t}^{2} \\\\ -4=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =2pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & =p{(-\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -5 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(-\\frac{4}{5}){t}^{2},\\,y=2(-\\frac{4}{5})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{4}{5}{t}^{2},\\,y=-\\frac{8}{5}t.\n$$" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285832 13194139534391 true] [17592186285831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285833 13194139534391 true] [17592186285831 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534391 true] [17592186285831 1041 "field-1" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285831 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285832 13194139534391 true] [17592186285831 1110 #uuid "9292f618-20fc-5f5b-b651-d46d9c09e736" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285832 1034 "-\\frac{4}{5}t^2" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285832 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285832 1111 #uuid "bed0c2b0-24f9-5ccd-aba1-0e03715b8e35" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285833 1034 "\\frac{4}{5}t^2" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285833 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285833 1111 #uuid "75c2fe08-1bcf-5695-a7cc-2aca55b78d5d" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285835 13194139534391 true] [17592186285834 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534391 true] [17592186285834 1041 "field-2" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285834 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285835 13194139534391 true] [17592186285834 1110 #uuid "146d0acb-1c7a-5699-899c-0a0fafd6cc94" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285835 1034 "-\\frac{8}{5}t" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285835 1111 #uuid "8960adf9-f3a6-585b-b81a-c530c948f3dc" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285836 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285837 13194139534391 true] [17592186285836 1089 "q-280365" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285836 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534391 true] [17592186285836 1100 "Consider the following parabola:\n\n$$\nx=-10{t}^{2},\\,y=-5t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the parabola is\n\n${y}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534391 true] [17592186285836 1113 #uuid "c403167e-2523-501b-884e-60c5c57d64a8" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285836 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =-\\frac{x}{10},\\,t=-\\frac{y}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{x}{10}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =-\\frac{x}{10} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{5}{2}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${y}^{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}x$" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285838 13194139534391 true] [17592186285837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285839 13194139534391 true] [17592186285837 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534391 true] [17592186285837 1041 "field-1" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285837 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285839 13194139534391 true] [17592186285837 1110 #uuid "27dffcb9-9fe1-517a-9f95-abcde23c2b86" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285838 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}x" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285838 1111 #uuid "8f04d4d4-2133-5dbc-a305-005aa794b32c" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285839 1034 "-\\frac{5}{2}x" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285839 1111 #uuid "a895497a-21cb-57fe-9900-9c04d3252d2e" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285840 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285841 13194139534391 true] [17592186285840 1089 "q-84674" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285840 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534391 true] [17592186285840 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997987/assets/671c38715438bb2a4b2ccf72a71765dadff1f2ed741ac52db7d4b70de43eee18.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285840 1113 #uuid "34a25ab3-e3bb-53ed-b1e5-0084906affac" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285840 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(2,-4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(2,-4),$ we can substitute $x=2$ and $y=-4$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2=2pt \\\\ -4=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2pt \\\\ 1 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =p{(\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(-\\frac{1}{4})t,\\,y=(-\\frac{1}{4}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285842 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285843 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285844 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285845 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285846 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1041 "selection" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285846 13194139534391 true] [17592186285841 1110 #uuid "3765f187-8258-5f3b-a4e2-95e68e6f1d94" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285842 1034 "x=t,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285842 1111 #uuid "35493562-7d30-56dc-b6ba-6ff2a9cd800a" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285843 1034 "x=8{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-8t" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285843 1111 #uuid "0728e5d9-c43b-58df-89f1-97fee14501b8" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285844 1034 "x=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-4t" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285844 1111 #uuid "c62885f3-8957-5e6f-815a-c14fce675bce" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285845 1034 "x=-t,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285845 1111 #uuid "34753177-4dac-5774-90ef-650d9e62bb43" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285846 1034 "x=-\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,\\,y=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534391 true] [17592186285846 1111 #uuid "5e0caedb-8a37-5dac-a5d9-5ba1678cbac4" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285847 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285848 13194139534391 true] [17592186285847 1089 "q-84675" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285847 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534391 true] [17592186285847 1100 "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point $(-7,-7)?$" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285847 1113 #uuid "51659ed2-0d6d-5995-abed-0cbe41395da6" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285847 1145 "The parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-7,-7),$ we can substitute $x=-7$ and $y=-7$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-7=2pt \\\\ -7=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7 & =2pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{7}{2p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7 & =p{(-\\frac{7}{2p})}^{2} \\\\ -7 & =p\\cdot \\frac{49}{4{p}^{2}} \\\\ -7 & =\\frac{49}{4p} \\\\ 4p & =-7 \\\\ p & =-\\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(-\\frac{7}{4})t,\\,y=(-\\frac{7}{4}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{7}{2}t,\\,y=-\\frac{7}{4}{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534391 true] [17592186285848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285849 13194139534391 true] [17592186285848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285850 13194139534391 true] [17592186285848 1